    "html": "<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.40 \\text{ kg}\"></span> sample of a substance undergoes a phase change from liquid to gas at a constant temperature of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"500 \\text{ K}\"></span>. The specific latent heat of vaporization of the substance is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5 \\times 10^5 \\text{ J kg}^{-1}\"></span>. What is the increase in entropy of the sample during this process?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0 \\times 10^2 \\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0 \\times 10^2 \\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0 \\times 10^5 \\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0 \\times 10^7 \\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
